course: dictionary
lesson: 7225
title: Photography: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Photography is the art, hobby or job of taking photographs with a camera or phone. Read the words around it to know which meaning is used. In «the film has beautiful photography», the clue is the film, so the word means the photos in it and how they were made.
explain: Photo means light, and graph means drawing or writing, so photography means drawing with light. That is how a camera works: light goes in and makes a picture. Scientists and artists both learn about this.
explain: Photography also has phrases. «Nature photography» and «wildlife photography» are about photos of plants and animals. «No flash photography» is a sign in a museum that tells you not to use a flash.
fact: Photography is the art, hobby or job of taking photographs.
fact: Photography can also mean the photos in a book, film or magazine, and how they are made.
fact: Photography began in the 1820s and 1830s.
fact: Napoleon, who died in 1821, was never photographed, but Abraham Lincoln and Taras Shevchenko were.
fact: Before you take or share a photo of someone else, ask them first. This is part of online safety.
exercise: «The film has beautiful photography.» In this sentence, what does photography mean? | *The photos in the film and how they were made | Drawing pictures by hand | A camera with a flash | Taking photos as a hobby
exercise: Which phrase means photos of animals in their wild homes? | Take up photography | No flash photography | Film photography | *Wildlife photography
exercise: Before you share a photo of a friend online, what should you do? | *Ask your friend first | Post it straight away | Send it to everyone in the class | Edit it so it looks different
test: In which decades did photography begin? | *1820s and 1830s | 1920s and 1930s | 1720s and 1730s
test: According to the example, who was never photographed? | *Napoleon | Abraham Lincoln | Taras Shevchenko
exam: Which word means the art, hobby or job of taking photographs with a camera or phone? | biography | *photography | geography
